  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/9682FC">Definition <span data-tag="9682FC">7.2.2.18</span>.</a>dimension!cohomologicalcohomoogical dimension Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos. We will say that $\calX $ has <em>cohomological dimension $\leq n$</em> if, for any sheaf of abelian groups $A$ on $\calX $, the cohomology group $\HH ^ k(\calX ,A)$ vanishes for $k > n$. </p>
